                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Spent maybe an hour with it before rolling credits, which tells you most of what you need to know. The controller support is basically a lie, my Xbox pad couldn't even navigate the menu, and the keyboard layout has you moving with arrows and shooting with WASD, which feels backwards every single second you play. I actually wanted to like the retro look, but the sprites are dull, the hitboxes are inconsistent, and having to install Java just to launch a 2D platformer in 2015 is its own kind of insult. Co-op sounded like the saving grace until one death sent both of us back to the stage start, and the fruit power ups don't even have working buttons mapped to them. There's a decent little idea buried here somewhere, but as it stands I'd rather replay something free.",
